Key provisions of 12 CFR § 1281.13 ('Special counting requirements'): (a) General. FHFA shall determine whether a Bank shall receive full, partial, or no credit toward achievement of any of the housing goals for a transaction that otherwise qualifies under this part. (b) Not counted. The following transactions or activities shall not be counted for purposes of the housing goals, meaning that in calculating the applicable percentage target level, they shall be excluded from both the numerator ( i.e., AMA mortgages acquired during the calendar year that are for very low-income families, low-income families, or families in low-income areas) and the denominator ( i.e., total AMA mortgages acquired during the calendar year), even if the transaction or activity would otherwise be counted under paragraph (c) of this section:
